---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
--- 

<MainLayout>

  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Patent Overview</h1>

    <p>
      The Dual Brain Robotics Architecture is the subject of a
      U.S. Utility-Provisional Patent Application.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>Current Status</h2>

    <p>
      A provisional patent application has been filed covering
      key aspects of the Dual Brain Robotics Architecture.
    </p>

    <p>
      Application No. 64/181,346
    </p>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>The Core Idea</h2>

    <p>
      The Dual Brain Robotics Architecture proposes a bilateral
      robotic control system inspired by the cooperative
      processing found in the human brain.
    </p>

    <p>
      Rather than relying on a single centralized control
      pathway, the architecture explores how two complementary
      cognitive systems can work together to support perception,
      prediction, adaptation, and motor coordination.
    </p>

    <p>
      A primary objective is improving robotic dexterity,
      micro-coordination, balance, and fluid movement in
      dynamic environments.
    </p>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>Why It Matters</h2>

    <p>
      Many robotic systems perform well in structured
      environments but struggle with fine motor control,
      adaptive movement, and real-world uncertainty.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Dual Brain Robotics Architecture explores whether
      bilateral cognitive processing can provide a foundation
      for more stable and adaptive robotic behavior.
    </p>

  </section>

</MainLayout>
